  <h2 id="context" class="scroll-mt-20">Overview</h2>
  <div class="not-prose grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 mt-6">
    <div>
      <p class="text-xs font-normal uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-2">Problem</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">Microsoft's consumer products operated as data silos. The project aimed to create a single account-level privacy notice, built on shared infrastructure, that remembers a user's choice across every Microsoft product. However, team members across disciplines had different motivations for, and understandings of, the project.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-xs font-normal uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-2">Solution</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">I introduced service blueprinting as a method to map how the user journey connected to each discipline, making the impact of every decision visible. I held ongoing workshops to align the team and promote unified decision-making.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-xs font-normal uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-2">Impact</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">Enabled cross-product personalization and intelligent recommendations through unified consent for over 2.2 billion users. Reached 800 million consented MAU across Windows, macOS, iOS, Android, and web.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Section timeline: inline on small screens, fixed beside the article on desktop -->
  <SectionNav items={[
    { id: 'context', label: 'Context' },
    { id: 'system', label: 'Mapping the system' },
    { id: 'research', label: 'Research' },
    { id: 'execution', label: 'Execution' },
